atlas.bailiff_appeal: description, inputSchema  -counterargument +counterargument, -refers -appeal to an independently vested Magistrate. No engine read +live Magistrate decides one question: does the return order stand as written? Yes: it stands. No: it -made. Until a vested Magistrate decides, the +vacated, stayed, or narrowed. Undecided: referred for deep review. The -DEEP_REVIEW_PENDING: Demonstration result, +a live demonstration ruling on a synthetic practice matter; it is -decided by any Magistrate. +certified and binds only this practice copy. -Demonstration on a synthetic practice matter; not certified; binds only this practice cop  parameters: -input.second_look
atlas.pulse_refer: description  -an independently vested +the demonstration -The referral goes to an independently vested Magistrate; until one rules, the result is DEEP_REVIEW_PENDING.
atlas.pulse_ruling: description  -vested -id once a vested Magistrate (O-VESTED-MAGISTRATE) has decided; until then it reports DEEP_REVIEW_PENDING ('Demonstration result, not decided by any Magistrate'). No +id. Demonstration: the -is +was +on this exact record by a separate Magistrate instance, did not read your AI's own wording, is not certified, -no engine decides. Not certified;
